## Where I believe the reviewer is wrong (not applied as written)

1. b6 — the row claims 017 §1 „Напротив, дори в договора да е записана спедиция“ is an inserted contrast marker
   with no counterpart in English. columns-en/017 line 37 does carry one: "Conversely, calling an arrangement
   freight forwarding or platform operations will not avoid regulation…". I applied the row's real point (the
   „Напротив“ = refutation calque) with „Обратно,“ instead of deleting the connector. The other two places the
   row names (017 FAQ/§1 "Warehousing, packing…" and 011 "Not every personal post…") genuinely have no marker in
   English and lost theirs.

2. b14 — the row states "016 is the only column that abbreviates the article; the other eight all write член in
   full (22 occurrences of чл. here against 34 of член elsewhere)". That is true only inside part b's scope
   (010–018). 002 (8 occurrences) and 007 (42) also wrote „чл.“, and part a did not flag them. I swept all three
   files so the whole set is consistent.

3. b12 — see the skip section: the U+200B characters are source parity, not a Bulgarian defect, and part a's
   reviewer had already re-checked and cleared them. Reported in round 4 for the same reason.

4. a19 — the row assumes 009's signature should be its own block "as every other column separates it". 003, 011,
   016 and 017 can separate it because their Korean sources have a matching block; 009's Korean has no signature
   line at all, so the separation cannot be made without breaking the block-count gate.

5. a20 / b13 / b17 (partial) — the suggested rewrites re-group thousands with spaces, which the checker's
   NUMBER_THOUSAND_STYLE.bg = 'dot' cannot parse; ACCEPTED-ROUND already rules those requests out.
